{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>To do him honor</b> — the king desires to do honor to him." "<b>And Haman said in his heart.</b> There is among the words of the individual [commentator] on this verse, namely that this scroll was written in prophecy, for who knows the hidden things of the heart except HaShem, who reveals His secret to His servants the prophets. And others said that it was by inference, or Haman revealed his secret afterward, or on that very day, and like it: ויאמר עשו בלבו. And the truth is that this scroll was written by ruach ha-kodesh. We find למי יחפוץ and also ודרכו יחפוץ — two mishqalim."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {1 "Resolved המגלה as 'this scroll' (the book of Esther); the phrase זאת המגלה appears twice, both referring to the megillah. The epithet 'the individual' likely refers to a specific earlier commentator but is left unresolved as Ibn Ezra does not name him."}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:11.155106289Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}